KG42.register("nodes-557ae67081a4dfc869f36dad",{"id":"KG31-b9a1f3b2c60ed604","code":"BID010.4","label":"Generation-component reporting separately from demand","definition":"Participants report the generation-side scheduling component and electricity demand separately to the organizer, retaining the original sign of the generation bid for supply aggregation and pricing; this component is not equivalent to the net supply quantity after offsetting local demand.","layer":"L3","template_code":"PGR","concept_id":"bidding.supply","concept_ids":["bidding.supply"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Submitting role: a participant reporting its own generation-side scheduling","Bid object: generation components listed separately from demand","Submission function: provide independent generation-side aggregation and pricing inputs"]},"exclusions":[["For each time period, generation and demand are reported separately; the generation bid keeps the original form e_{gen,t}^bid=x_t^{dis*}η^{dis}−P_{PV,t}, t∈T.","It includes the EV discharge term and the PV term, retaining the original A24 sign; the discharge efficiency η^{dis} and PV power are retained according to the specific resource configuration.","Subsequent pricing is aggregated as Σ_n|e_{gen,n,t}^bid|, without rewriting the bid itself as a positive number."]],"members":[{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","market_meaning":"The supply component must report generation separately from demand in the submitted energy bid, rather than reporting only overall net demand. Scope: MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]},"constraint_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C001","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"bfab9666b53fd722f3c15f0a17dcc5ac066bd684056f6a57b9098a5c56122344","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012","node_id":"bidding.supply","function":"bidding.supply","unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","anchor":true},{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R014","market_meaning":"Submitted generation quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. Submitted demand quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. The coordinator calculates internal prices using the MMR pricing model. Scope: MMR pricing within one energy sharing region. The internal buying and selling prices are equal to the arithmetic mean of the retailer's export and retail prices. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation equals total demand. The internal selling price remains the arithmetic mean of export and retail prices; the internal buying price is adjusted to cover the regional deficit imported at the retailer's retail price. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation is less than total demand. The internal buying price remains the arithmetic mean of export and retail prices; the internal selling price is adjusted to incorporate surplus-export income for distribution among participants providing electricity through generation or EV discharging. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation exceeds total demand.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. | MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. | MMR pricing within one energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},"constraint_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::v141-c-R014-C001"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"a224bf63fdbdff5bed026ae7e29a057b5ec0c0bbb01e1bf9b93de0d872bafc47","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014","node_id":"bidding.supply","function":"bidding.supply","unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A24","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A24","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R014","quote":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-07","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A25-A27","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids of all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal price in different ways according to the relationship between total generation and demand in the energy sharing region. If the generation is equal to demand, the internal buying and selling price are equal, taking the average of the export and retail price:\n\np_t^{buy} = p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} = \\frac{(r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})}{2}, \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| = \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A25)\n\nIf the generation is less than demand, the deficit generation has to be supplied by the power imported from the retailer at the retail price, and the cost of this import should be covered. Therefore, in this situation, the internal selling price keeps the same as that in Formula (A25), but the buying price is modified:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\right) \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \u003c \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A26)\n\nSimilarly, if the generation is higher than demand, the surplus generation needs to be sold to the retailer at the export price, and this part of income needs to be distributed among all the prosumers who provide electricity by generation or EV discharging. The internal price is calculated as follows:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{average} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\right) \\cdot r_t^{export}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}|} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| > \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A27)\n\nFormulas (A25)-(A27) compose the pricing model in the coordinator agent under mid-market rate mechanism.","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R014","quote":"With the energy bids of all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal price in different ways according to the relationship between total generation and demand in the energy sharing region. If the generation is equal to demand, the internal buying and selling price are equal, taking the average of the export and retail price:\n\np_t^{buy} = p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} = \\frac{(r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})}{2}, \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| = \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A25)\n\nIf the generation is less than demand, the deficit generation has to be supplied by the power imported from the retailer at the retail price, and the cost of this import should be covered. Therefore, in this situation, the internal selling price keeps the same as that in Formula (A25), but the buying price is modified:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\right) \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \u003c \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A26)\n\nSimilarly, if the generation is higher than demand, the surplus generation needs to be sold to the retailer at the export price, and this part of income needs to be distributed among all the prosumers who provide electricity by generation or EV discharging. The internal price is calculated as follows:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{average} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\right) \\cdot r_t^{export}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}|} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| > \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A27)\n\nFormulas (A25)-(A27) compose the pricing model in the coordinator agent under mid-market rate mechanism."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["separate_generation_quantity_submission"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG31-L3-SC-L3-2ff544e3ec16c9d0","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L3","ontological_kind":"SC-L3-2ff544e3ec16c9d0"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"Participants report the generation-side scheduling component and electricity demand separately to the organizer, retaining the original sign of the generation bid for supply aggregation and pricing; this component is not equivalent to the net supply quantity after offsetting local demand.","identity_fields":["Submitting role: a participant reporting its own generation-side scheduling","Bid object: generation components listed separately from demand","Submission function: provide independent generation-side aggregation and pricing inputs"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply","paper_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","function":"bidding.supply","source_occurrences":[{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","market_meaning":"The supply component must report generation separately from demand in the submitted energy bid, rather than reporting only overall net demand. Scope: MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]},"constraint_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C001","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"bfab9666b53fd722f3c15f0a17dcc5ac066bd684056f6a57b9098a5c56122344"},{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::V::bidding.supply","rule_id":"v141-c-R014","market_meaning":"Submitted generation quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. Submitted demand quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. The coordinator calculates internal prices using the MMR pricing model. Scope: MMR pricing within one energy sharing region. The internal buying and selling prices are equal to the arithmetic mean of the retailer's export and retail prices. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation equals total demand. The internal selling price remains the arithmetic mean of export and retail prices; the internal buying price is adjusted to cover the regional deficit imported at the retailer's retail price. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation is less than total demand. The internal buying price remains the arithmetic mean of export and retail prices; the internal selling price is adjusted to incorporate surplus-export income for distribution among participants providing electricity through generation or EV discharging. Scope: MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. Condition: Total generation exceeds total demand.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"MMR internal prices at a given time step within one energy sharing region. | MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step. | MMR pricing within one energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},"constraint_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::v141-c-R014-C001"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"a224bf63fdbdff5bed026ae7e29a057b5ec0c0bbb01e1bf9b93de0d872bafc47"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The supply component must report generation separately from demand in the submitted energy bid, rather than reporting only overall net demand. Scope: MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"],"ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A24","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"In the MMR mechanism, the generation (supply) component of the energy bid at time step t is defined as the EV discharging power times the discharging efficiency minus the PV power output: e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} η^{dis}) - P_{PV,t} for all t ∈ T.","expression":"e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R012-V001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R012-P001","v141-c-R012-P002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"],"ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A24","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R014-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted generation quantities are inputs to internal-price calculation according to regional total generation relative to demand. Scope: MMR internal pricing within one energy sharing region, using separate generation and demand submissions at each time step.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["e_gen_bid_nt"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"],"ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::v141-c-R014-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R014","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A24","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-07","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A25-A27","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids of all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal price in different ways according to the relationship between total generation and demand in the energy sharing region. If the generation is equal to demand, the internal buying and selling price are equal, taking the average of the export and retail price:\n\np_t^{buy} = p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} = \\frac{(r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})}{2}, \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| = \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A25)\n\nIf the generation is less than demand, the deficit generation has to be supplied by the power imported from the retailer at the retail price, and the cost of this import should be covered. Therefore, in this situation, the internal selling price keeps the same as that in Formula (A25), but the buying price is modified:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\right) \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \u003c \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A26)\n\nSimilarly, if the generation is higher than demand, the surplus generation needs to be sold to the retailer at the export price, and this part of income needs to be distributed among all the prosumers who provide electricity by generation or EV discharging. The internal price is calculated as follows:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{average} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\right) \\cdot r_t^{export}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}|} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| > \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A27)\n\nFormulas (A25)-(A27) compose the pricing model in the coordinator agent under mid-market rate mechanism."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R012-V001","symbol":"x_t^{dis*}","meaning":"discharging power variable of the EV at time step t (denoted x_t^{dis*} in the generation component of the MMR energy bid)","kind":"operational","domain":"power quantity per time step t ∈ T (domain not specified in the cited A24 snippet)","unit":null,"indices":["t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::x::v141-c-R012-V001"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R012-P001","symbol":"η^{dis}","meaning":"discharging efficiency parameter multiplying x_t^{dis*} in the generation component of the MMR energy bid","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-P001"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R012-P002","symbol":"P_{PV,t}","meaning":"PV power output at time step t, subtracted from the discharging output in the generation component of the MMR energy bid","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::theta::v141-c-R012-P002"},{"parameter_id":"e_gen_bid_nt","symbol":"e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}","meaning":"Generation-component energy bid submitted by prosumer n at time step t under MMR; an exogenous input to this pricing rule (determined by the bidding/decision model), entering the internal-price formulas only through the regional total of its absolute value, Σ_{n∈PA}|e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}|. Scoped here as pricing input, not as a decision of pricing.local.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06","v141-b-g07-ev-07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R014","declaration_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::theta::e_gen_bid_nt"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply","stage":"L3","subtype":"separate_generation_quantity_submission","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"For each time period, the generation component and demand component are reported separately; the generation bid follows the original form e_{gen,t}^bid=x_t^{dis*}η^{dis}−P_{PV,t}, t∈T.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: the generation bid sequence listed separately from demand","Core relationship: independently report generation components","Output: e_{gen,t}^bid"],"variation_fields":["The generation component includes the EV discharge term and the PV term, maintaining the original A24 sign","The discharge efficiency η^{dis} and PV power are retained according to the specific resource configuration","Subsequent pricing is aggregated as Σ_n|e_{gen,n,t}^bid|, and the bid itself is not rewritten as a positive number"],"constraint_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C001","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C002","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R014::v141-c-R014-C001"],"paper_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","function":"bidding.supply","template_code":"PGR"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply","retained_variants":["For each time period, generation and demand are reported separately; the generation bid keeps the original form e_{gen,t}^bid=x_t^{dis*}η^{dis}−P_{PV,t}, t∈T.","It includes the EV discharge term and the PV term, retaining the original A24 sign; the discharge efficiency η^{dis} and PV power are retained according to the specific resource configuration.","Subsequent pricing is aggregated as Σ_n|e_{gen,n,t}^bid|, without rewriting the bid itself as a positive number."],"evidence_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-666e540de295773e","baseline_parent_code":"BID010","secondary_class":"SC-L3-2ff544e3ec16c9d0","category":{"id":"SC-L3-2ff544e3ec16c9d0","stage":"L3","label_zh":"Reporting of separately listed generation quantities","definition_zh":"Participants report the generation-side scheduling component and electricity demand separately to the organizer, retaining the original sign of the generation bid for supply aggregation and pricing; this component is not equivalent to the net supply quantity after offsetting local demand.","main_identity_axes":["Participant role reporting its own generation-side scheduling","Generation components independent of the demand bid","Function of providing generation-side aggregation and pricing inputs"],"inclusion_criteria":["The source explicitly requires that generation components and demand components be reported separately.","The reported object is the generation-side scheduling component, used for supply aggregation or pricing.","The original bid sign and subsequent statistical operations such as taking absolute values are retained separately."],"exclusion_criteria":["Reporting of net supply components after offsetting demand.","Electricity sale quotes, orders, or proposals expressing intention to accept or match transactions.","Consumption demand reporting, regulation service supply, and exemption-from-reporting rules."],"supporting_unit_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"Participants report the generation-side scheduling component and electricity demand separately to the organizer, retaining the original sign of the generation bid for supply aggregation and pricing; this component is not equivalent to the net supply quantity after offsetting local demand.","identity_fields":["Submitting role: a participant reporting its own generation-side scheduling","Bid object: generation components listed separately from demand","Submission function: provide independent generation-side aggregation and pricing inputs"],"member_unit_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M02::bidding.supply"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/326"});
